A||||10||87FieroGT||Painting suggestions??||||1||
Z||000000||87FieroGT||12-07-1999||12:43 AM||||I am going to be repainting my car next year and I need some suggestions about paint schemes. I know that I will be painting the same color as the purple on the plymoth prowler. I need to know if it would look better if I keep the two tone color and the side moldings black or make the car mono cromatic like all the newer cars. I would love to hear any opinions. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||2FAST4U||12-07-1999||02:01 AM||||You can paint it any color you want to as long as it's red||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||12-07-1999||02:53 AM||||How about a nice primer color?||||reg||10
Z||000003||kel||12-07-1999||05:07 AM||||Personally, I like the contrasting colors.  Maybe I'm just more used to it on Fieros, but I really think it sets off whatever color you use for the body.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mutfish||12-07-1999||07:25 AM||||In my opinion,a single color paint scheme will give it a lower look. The Prowler purple sounds slick. Just repainted my '88 GT black(was orig. white)but might have gone with the purple....if I'd thought of it.....||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sage||12-07-1999||08:26 AM||||The car is too small to be all one color and look as good as it could. The natural line that Pontiac put in(at the bottom) lends itself well to a contrasting color. That is a pretty neat color on the Prowler though. It depends on what wheels you will be running but how about the silver as a second color around the bottom?  Are you base-coat clear-coating it, or going acrylic enamel?||||reg||6
Z||000006||Phil||12-07-1999||10:12 AM||||I just went through the color choice bit myself on my Formula. Red (original color ) was not even in the running. Pearl white or metallic blue surfaced for awhile (my 88 GT is met blue), finally wound up with Corvette Competition Yellow with or without graphics design (still working on the wife for that one the graphics I mean) Hey whatever floats your boat. You only have to please yourself nobody else ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||12-07-1999||12:32 PM||||One of the guys in our club just had his 86 SE (notchback, with GT lower cladding) painted dark emerald green. Had the cladding painted green, as well. Looks great!  Especially with gray GT diamond-spokes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gokart||12-07-1999||08:52 PM||||Make sure not to paint the mouldings. I hate seeing hack's painting the moulding! I would paint the gray ground effects black w/purple.||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||12-07-1999||09:54 PM||||Personally, I think the mono paint schemes are overdone and overrated.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||12-07-1999||11:38 PM||||The reds are more expensive paints.  I just checked on colors for my car.  I picked Dupont BM142.  It's called a "saturated blue metallic" although it looks alot more purple than blue.  Stay away from the actual "Prowler Purple".  Find a color from DuPont or somebody that matches.  If you go to Plymouth and ask for a couple pints of that color you will pay alot.  Prowler purple (or whatever Plymouth actually calls it) probably hasn't been released yet except to the dealers.  I'm rambling...I'll quit.||||reg||1
